  "scope": "Hackdirt launcher shop performance, normal controls and native save/restart; the full Hackdirt quest course remains open.",
  "diagnoses": [
    "Repeated no-op Enable/Disable commands scanned every resident cell and saved reference.",
    "Standalone GetDisabled queries allocated/sorted an entire saved-world index.",
    "Offscreen door planning searched thousands of unrelated cells and routed to ineligible or dominated door candidates.",
    "Fresh offscreen actors shared the same 250 ms deadline, concentrating startup planning in one frame.",
    "Retained debug executables in tmpfs /tmp exhausted its per-user quota and competed for RAM/swap."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Skip enable-parent reconciliation for unchanged script writes; retain propagation for changed roots.",
    "Use a linear parent-chain lookup for standalone enable queries; retain shared indexed batch queries and stale-storage rejection.",
    "Bound reverse door search at validated source exits and their directed street frontiers; constrain same-cell bridges before routing.",
    "Order candidate cells by distance within door-hop priority and conservatively reject routes whose straight-line lower bound exceeds the best validated route cost.",
    "Distribute fresh actor deadlines across the existing 250 ms cadence, preserving saved deadlines on restore.",
    "Keep independent retained tryouts on user storage under ~/.local/state/openmw-oblivion/tryouts."
  ],
